{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"submissive-prettied-hawk","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n`scripts/check_config_reads.py` proves every `_config_schema.py` field is consumed somewhere, but nothing proves the OPPOSITE direction: that ONLY approved composition roots/provider boundaries read ambient configuration and credentials. Without that, a new ambient `load_config`/`os.getenv` read below the central seam can silently reappear or a new credential name can be introduced with no owner.\n\n## Outcome\nA new deterministic AST gate `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` (mirroring the existing gate's `check(root)->list[str]` / `main(argv)->int` contract and `# read-via:` escape-marker style) flags any direct or import/local-aliased `load_config`, `os.getenv`, `os.environ.get`, `os.environ[...]`, literal-`getattr` env equivalent, backend property reload, credential read, or configurable adapter default that occurs BELOW the approved seams. An explicit registry enumerates the approved composition roots and provider-credential boundaries, derived from the authoritative config/adapter registries, and the gate fails when a newly declared configurable env spelling or provider credential name has no owner. Test-only controls and protocol constants are allowed only via exact `path + symbol + rationale` entries (never broad path globs). An initial legacy-exception set enumerates the current real-tree violations as exact entries so the gate is introducible without yet touching product code; slice C3 drains that set to empty.\n\n## Plan\n1. Implement the AST gate: receiver/alias resolution to classify each ambient access, an approved-seam/owner registry (module or data file), and a diagnostic that reports `path`, `symbol`, `access kind`, and `owning seam`.\n2. Encode the initial legacy-exception set as exact `path+symbol+rationale` entries covering every current below-seam read so the real tree passes; forbid path-glob exceptions structurally.\n3. Author synthetic red-proof fixtures and self-tests.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Synthetic fixture modules for direct, import-aliased, and local-aliased call forms and every prohibited env-access form (attribute, subscript, `.get`, literal-`getattr`) each fail the gate with the expected `path/symbol/access-kind/owning-seam` diagnostic.\n- Self-tests that deliberately insert a new bypass, a new unowned registry name, a broad path-glob exception, or a missing rationale each fail with the expected diagnostic.\n- Clean approved fixtures (reads inside a registered seam) pass with no findings.\n- The gate runs deterministically OFFLINE with no network or CI dependency: `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` exits 0 on the current tree and 1 when a synthetic violation is present.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nAdditive: the gate is not yet wired into `make lint`/CI (slice C2) and product code is unchanged (slice C3). Rollback deletes the script, registry, and fixtures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every synthetic prohibited access/alias/default/exception and unowned-new-registry-name fixture fails the gate with `path`, `symbol`, `access kind`, and expected owning seam; clean approved fixtures pass.\n- [ ] The registry maps each approved read to exactly one seam; a newly declared configurable env spelling or provider-credential name lacking an owner fails the gate; path-glob exceptions are rejected structurally.\n- [ ] The gate exposes the `check(root) -> list[str]` and `main(argv) -> int` contract and is unit-tested; it runs deterministically offline with no CI/network dependency and exits 0 on the current tree.","id":"29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8","parent_id":"aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 S7.1 — Config-ownership AST gate + approved-owner registry + red-proof fixtures"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787081599804901001,"uuid":"a847227d-36ef-4563-ae48-7d92d5b8b822"}